        setup: {
          players: '2 players (this variant). Also commonly 4 in partnerships or 4 individuals; rules are the same.',
          deck: 'Standard 52-card pack (French suits, no jokers). Pişti uses the full deck: four cards are dealt face down to the centre, four to each player, and the remainder forms the stock; one centre card is turned face up to start the pile.',
          equipment: '',
          dealing: "Dealer shuffles; player to dealer's left cuts. Dealer deals 4 cards face down to the center, then 4 to each player. Remaining cards form the stock. One of the four center cards is turned face up to start the pile (if it is a Jack, turn until a non-Jack). Player to dealer's right plays first. After all play their 4 cards, dealer deals 4 more to each from stock; repeat until stock is exhausted.",
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first to reach 151 points (or first team in partnership play). If both reach 151 on the same hand, the higher score wins.',
          gameplay: "Each turn, play one card from your hand face up onto the center pile. If your card's rank matches the top card of the pile, you capture the whole pile; playing a Jack also captures the pile regardless of the top card. Otherwise your card stays on the pile. The first capture also takes the four face-down center cards. When everyone has played their four cards, the dealer deals four more to each from the stock; play continues until the stock is exhausted. The last team or player to make a capture takes any remaining cards. Score after each hand; first to 151 wins.",
          keyRules: [
            'Match the rank of the top card to capture the pile, or play a Jack to capture any pile.',
            'First capture also takes the four face-down center cards.',
            'Pişti: capturing a single card with a matching rank (not Jack) scores 10 bonus points; Jack on single Jack is double pişti (20 points). No pişti on the very first or very last card of the hand.',
            'Points: Jack 1, Ace 1, 2 of Clubs 2, 10 of Diamonds 3, majority of cards 3, each pişti 10 (double pişti 20).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Keep track of the Jacks! Since the Jack is a wild capture, don't drop a high-point card (like the 10 of Diamonds) into the center if your opponent hasn't played their Jacks yet. If you have the same rank as the top card, play it immediatelyâ€”don't 'Save' it, because the opponent might play a Jack and steal your match.",
          intermediate: "The 'Pişti' Setup: If you are the first player and the center card is something you have in your hand (e.g., an 8 is showing and you have an 8), play it. If the next person doesn't have an 8 or a Jack, you have a high chance of scoring a Pişti on your next turn. Memory is key: remember which ranks have been 'Clear' so you don't drop a card that can be 'Pish-teed'.",
          advanced: "The 'Endgame Vacuum': The winner of the very last trick gets all remaining cards in the center. In the final round of dealing, save your Jacks for the final two cards. This ensures that even if you didn't match anything mid-round, you can 'Sweep' the table for the 'Most Cards' bonus, which is often the tie-breaker for the 151 goal.",
          tips: [
            "The 10 of Diamonds (3 pts) and 2 of Clubs (2 pts) are the 'Gold' cards. Protect them!",
            "If you suspect your opponent has a Jack, lead a 'Low' card (like a 4 or 5) to lure their Jack out on a useless pile.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
